# MASTER DEVELOPMENT PROMPT: COMPREHENSIVE STRESS, ANXIETY & DEPRESSION ASSESSMENT AND MENTAL WELLNESS WEB APPLICATION

## 1. PROJECT OVERVIEW

Act as a world-class multidisciplinary software development team comprising:

- A Senior Product Manager.
- A Senior UI/UX Designer.
- A Clinical Psychologist.
- A Consultant Psychiatrist.
- A Medical Doctor.
- A Mental Health Research Specialist.
- A Senior Frontend Engineer.
- A Senior Software Architect.
- A Quality Assurance Engineer.
- A Cybersecurity and Privacy Specialist.
- An Accessibility Specialist.

Your responsibility is to plan, architect, design, develop, test and deliver a production-quality, responsive, browser-based mental health screening and wellness application.

The application will focus on three interconnected but distinct areas of mental health:

1. Stress.
2. Anxiety.
3. Depression.

The primary purpose is to enable individuals to complete structured mental health assessments using clinically informed questions, relevant personal and lifestyle information, and validated screening instruments where appropriate.

Based on the information supplied by the user, the application should evaluate reported symptoms, estimate their severity, identify potential warning signs, explain the assessment results and provide personalized, evidence-informed recommendations.

The application should also serve as a comprehensive mental wellness educational platform, providing reliable information, practical self-help resources, coping strategies, lifestyle recommendations and guidance on when to seek professional medical attention.

**Product vision:** Build a reliable, intelligent, accessible and visually exceptional mental wellness platform that helps people understand their psychological well-being and make informed decisions about their mental health.

This is a screening, educational and wellness-support application. It is NOT a diagnostic medical device and must never present its results as a confirmed medical diagnosis.

## 2. PROJECT CONSTRAINTS AND TECHNICAL REQUIREMENTS

The following requirements are mandatory:

- Application type: Browser-based web application.
- Authentication: None.
- User registration: None.
- Database: None.
- Backend: Avoid requiring a backend for core functionality.
- Data persistence: No remote storage of assessment answers or personal health information.
- Architecture: Client-side application.
- Responsive design: Fully responsive across desktop, laptop, tablet and mobile devices.
- Navigation: Professional top navigation bar.
- Footer: Comprehensive footer containing relevant navigation and informational links.
- UI/UX: Premium, modern, clean, intuitive and professional.
- Accessibility: Follow WCAG 2.2 AA principles.
- Performance: Optimize loading speed, responsiveness and rendering.
- Security: Apply secure frontend development practices.
- Maintainability: Use modular, reusable and well-organized code.
- Scalability: Structure the application so that future features can be added without rebuilding the entire application.
- Testing: Include unit, integration, functional and end-to-end testing.
- Browser compatibility: Support current versions of Chrome, Firefox, Safari and Edge.

Do not introduce authentication, database integration, subscriptions, payment gateways or unnecessary backend infrastructure.

The application must work independently in the browser.

All assessment calculations should be performed locally using deterministic, transparent and testable logic.

Do not send assessment answers to external AI services or third-party APIs.

Where practical, assessment answers should remain in memory only and disappear when the session is closed or the user resets the assessment.

## 3. TARGET AUDIENCE

Design the application for:

- Adults experiencing everyday stress.
- Individuals experiencing persistent anxiety symptoms.
- People who may be experiencing depressive symptoms.
- Students and young professionals.
- Working professionals and entrepreneurs.
- Individuals experiencing emotional or psychological difficulties.
- People interested in understanding and improving their mental wellness.
- Individuals who want to conduct an initial self-assessment before consulting a healthcare professional.

The initial screening experience should be designed for adults aged 18 and above.

If minors access the application, clearly explain that the adult screening tools are not intended for them and direct them to appropriate support from a qualified healthcare professional or trusted adult.

